\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 ## TL;DR\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 - **Up Collective is a UK startup-marketing services group**, owned by Copy Club Ltd (UK Co. No. 11449958, Shelton Street, Covent Garden, London) and led by founder/CEO Lottie Unwin. It is the parent of three sister brands \'97 **Up World** (community + training), **Brand Hackers** (fractional marketing agency) and **Up Talent** (marketing recruitment) \'97 all targeting the same audience: people who do (or hire) marketing inside UK start-ups and scale-ups.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 - **Olivia Pike is the Community and Operations Manager at Up World** (the Up Collective's community brand), based in London/Bristol. Her LinkedIn self-description ("Hi, I'm Olivia \uc0\u55357 \u56395 \u55356 \u57340 , Community and Operations at Up World \'96 a community that will change\'85") and RocketReach record confirm the title; the Up World "About Us" page lists her as "Olivia \'96 Community Executive" with a bio noting she is "in Bristol crocheting her next project," consistent with a recent step up from Community Executive to Community & Operations Manager.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 - **Positioning is distinctive in three ways**: (1) an explicitly *friendly, informal "marketing mates"* tone (anti-corporate, slightly irreverent \'97 Brand Hackers' tagline is "no corporate cringe"); (2) a tight **B2C/DTC start-up vertical focus** with named challenger-brand clients (Tony's Chocolonely, Lucky Saint, Pip & Nut, Who Gives A Crap, Wednesday's Domaine, Dr Will's, etc.); and (3) a stated mission overlay \'97 each Up Collective brand pledges to donate 2% of revenue (Up World/Brand Hackers cite the Laadli Boarding Home / Sambhali Trust in Jodhpur, with Brand Hackers also citing Luminary Bakery).\cb1 \
