\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 ### 1. The Company and the Three Brands\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 \'a0\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 **Up Collective (the-up-collective.co)** is the umbrella holding company. Its homepage states verbatim: *"The Up Collective unlocks the power of marketing for startups\'85 We're the powerhouse behind Up World, Up Talent & Brand Hackers."* It is operated by **Copy Club Ltd** (the legal entity \'97 visible in the Brand Hackers website footer: "\'a92025 Copy Club Ltd T/A Brand Hackers") with **Companies House number 11449958** (shown in the Up World site footer). Registered address: **Shelton Street, Covent Garden, London, WC2H 9JQ**. The group was founded by **Lottie Unwin**, a former Procter & Gamble assistant brand manager and former Head of Marketing at PROPERCORN; it started as a supper club / micro-community called **The Copy Club** around 2018\'962019 and rebranded the community arm to **Up World** as the wider Up Collective ecosystem was built out (multiple podcast interviews with Unwin on Out of Hours, People Doing Things, Badass Unicorn, Your Basket Is Empty, Bunch, and Keep Optimising).\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 \'a0\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 The three operating brands:\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 \'a0\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 **A) Up World (up-world.co)** \'97 *"Community & training services for ambitious startup marketers."* Up World is itself a portfolio of products:\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 - **Up Club** \'97 paid Slack-based membership for marketers, freelancers, agencies and in-house teams. Up World's "For Marketers" page cites *"over 1,078 UK marketers"* and the home page states *"over 1,100 paying members."*\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 - **Big Up Club** \'97 *"invite-only community designed for start-up Marketing Directors, Heads of Marketing, and CMOs"*; the FAQ confirms it is **explicitly focused on B2C brands** with cohorts of 20 new members every three months.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 - **The Marketing Accelerator, Brand Manager Bootcamp, How To Be A Great Manager** \'97 paid courses.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 - **Mentor Matching** \'97 pairs members with senior marketing mentors.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 - **Up Fest** \'97 a one-day "green-field" marketing festival held outside London (transport options listed from London Paddington to Oxford and London Waterloo to Haslemere in recent years).\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 - **The Marketing Hustle** \'97 the group's podcast (linked from Brand Hackers and Up World LinkedIn).\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 \'a0\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 **B) Brand Hackers (brand-hackers.co)** \'97 *"Helping challengers fight smarter, think sharper, and win bigger."* Positioned as a **fractional marketing agency / "secret growth partner"**, not an ad agency. Public claims on the site: **300+ brands supported, 65 million+ social views driven, 5 years in operation, ~20+ staff** (per a careers ad: *"4 years old and have grown from just 2 of us to 20+ people"*). Verifiable clients on the home page or case studies include **Tony's Chocolonely, Lucky Saint, Bol Foods, Here We Flo, Who Gives A Crap, TimTams, Wednesday's Domaine (CAC cut 49% in 2 months \'97 case study), Gerry Anderson (84% ROAS, 182% YoY revenue), Dr Will's (10,000 bottles sold in Tesco), PARLA (rate-of-sale +74% in Sainsbury's), MdLondon, Pip & Nut, Rocketo, Rock Face, TRIP, The Curators, OTO, Seep, Super Nonna and Islands Chocolate**. Industries served listed are Beauty & Wellness, Food & Drink, Luxury Goods, Film & Media, Fashion & Retail, Health & Fitness, Software & Apps and Pet Care. Three customer archetypes are explicitly named: **founder-led startups, post-funding scale-ups, and "big corps acting as challengers."** Two physical hubs are listed: Huckletree Oxford Circus (London) and Huckletree Ancoats St (Manchester); the team is otherwise remote.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 \'a0\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 **C) Up Talent (up-talent.co)** \'97 *"Your startup marketing recruitment & careers partners."* Run by Lottie Unwin and "Talent Partner" Laura (10 years of recruitment experience including in-house at Essence Mediacom). The site uses the language *"Match Making"* rather than "recruitment", aimed at first marketing hires through to senior team-builds. Self-reported scale: *"1,000+ start-up marketers in our Community, 8,456 e-mail subscribers, 20,600 average visits to our careers page monthly, 12,944 Marketers on our Database."* Hook line: *"The average bad hire in marketing costs \'a338k."* Named client references on the site include **work.life, Urban Legend, The Roost, Peters Yard, Live Link, Karma Drinks, Momo, Pip & Nut and Nice Drinks**.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 \'a0\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 > The three brands operate as a tightly cross-referenced ecosystem: Up Talent describes itself as *"part of the Up World group"*; the Brand Hackers footer notes the legal entity is Copy Club Ltd; and Up World's careers page (careers.up-world.co) hosts vacancies across all three.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 \'a0\cb1 \
