\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 ### 2. The Market\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 \'a0\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 **Industry:** UK **start-up / scale-up marketing services** \'97 sitting at the intersection of three traditionally separate verticals: paid professional community/membership, fractional marketing services (a sub-segment of management consulting / agency), and specialist talent recruitment.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 \'a0\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 **Target customer (per the brands' own segmentation):**\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 - *Marketers in start-ups* \'97 from graduate/junior through to CMO. Up Club's "For Marketers", "For Freelancers", "For Agencies" and "For Marketing Teams" pages each address a distinct audience.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 - *Marketing Directors / Heads of Marketing / CMOs of B2C start-ups* \'97 addressed by Big Up Club (explicitly B2C only).\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 - *Start-up founders* needing a first marketing hire or fractional team \'97 addressed by Up Talent and Brand Hackers.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 - *Established "big corps" wanting challenger thinking* \'97 addressed by Brand Hackers as a third archetype.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 \'a0\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 **Problem being solved (in their own words):**\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 - Isolation and lack of development support inside start-ups. Lottie Unwin's quote, repeated across all three brand sites: *"My crash landing into start-up marketing was thrilling & inspiring but brutally lonely. Over the years I've needed marketing mates, I've needed recruiters who understand me and my career and support to truly get sh*t done."*\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 - A Community Executive job ad puts it more bluntly: *"we create a space that's desperately needed for individuals who, without us, don't have any structured personal development, can't reach their full potential, and often find professional life very lonely."*\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 - For founders/hirers, the framing is risk-of-bad-hire (the \'a338k figure) and lack of true start-up understanding from generalist agencies.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 \'a0\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
