\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 **Tone and voice.** Across all three brand sites the voice is deliberately informal, warm and self-aware. Recurring lexicon includes "marketing mates," "smashing your goals," "marketing superstars," "kick-ass," and the slightly cheeky "Hackers" framing. Brand Hackers explicitly positions against corporate slickness: *"We won't send you generic 'insights' you could get from AI LinkedIn gurus\'85 actual marketing advice that works for free (with zero corporate cringe)."* An Up Fest testimonial cited on the Up World site captures the cultural positioning: *"Up World truly is underpinned by a philosophy of showing kindness and being empathetic \'96 i.e. being human. Everyone showed up as humans first, professionals second."*\cb1 \
